From: daedalao <daedalao@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] SWGL: big-endian swizzle only for X11, not Wayland

0007 swizzles SWGL's B8G8R8A8 frames to the A8R8G8B8 memory layout on
big-endian because X11 consumes native-endian pixel values. On Wayland the
frame is attached as WL_SHM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, which is little-endian, i.e.
already the B8G8R8A8 layout, so the swizzle swapped red and blue (and moved
alpha). Skip it when the GDK display is Wayland.

Tested: Arch POWER powerpc64 (BE), river/wlroots pixman, software WebRender:
colour stripes correct on both X11 (Xwayland) and Wayland.
---
--- a/gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorSWGL.cpp	2026-09-26 10:12:52.812048800 -0700
+++ b/gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorSWGL.cpp	2026-09-26 10:12:52.830419078 -0700
@@ -215,7 +215,17 @@
   wr_swgl_init_default_framebuffer(mContext, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, nullptr);
   // If we have a draw target at this point, mapping must have succeeded.
   MOZ_ASSERT(mMappedData != nullptr);
-  if (aDirty && std::endian::native != std::endian::little) {
+  bool swizzleForNativeEndian =
+      aDirty && std::endian::native != std::endian::little;
+#ifdef MOZ_WIDGET_GTK
+  // Only X11 consumes native-endian pixel values. On Wayland the buffer is
+  // attached as WL_SHM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, which is little-endian: exactly the
+  // B8G8R8A8 layout SWGL resolved, so it must be left alone.
+  if (widget::GdkIsWaylandDisplay()) {
+    swizzleForNativeEndian = false;
+  }
+#endif
+  if (swizzleForNativeEndian) {
     // SWGL resolves pixels in the little-endian B8G8R8A8 memory layout, but
     // the window surface consumes native-endian 32-bit pixel values, so on
     // big-endian rewrite to the A8R8G8B8 memory layout. Only the dirty
